WEBVTT

00:00.170 --> 00:05.360
Once in a long life, a star
with a tail comes back.

00:05.400 --> 00:08.200
When it comes back, will you be here?

00:08.550 --> 00:09.600
I'll be here.

00:09.867 --> 00:11.007
Promise?

00:11.292 --> 00:12.292
Promise.

00:12.542 --> 00:13.712
Don't be late.

00:13.862 --> 00:15.052
I'm a tortoise.

00:15.092 --> 00:16.102
[laughs]

00:16.242 --> 00:17.422
[laughs]

00:17.312 --> 00:18.512
[hums]

00:25.325 --> 00:28.025
SEVENTY-SIX SUMMERS

00:30.325 --> 00:32.135
Morning, boulder! Where you headed?

00:32.385 --> 00:36.385
The standing stone. Tonight.

00:36.725 --> 00:39.405
At this speed? You'll
get there next spring!

00:39.445 --> 00:40.975
[laughs]

00:41.158 --> 00:44.088
Then he'll be seventy-five years
early for the next comet.

00:44.958 --> 00:49.678
When the standing stone goes
dark, the comet blooms.

00:49.858 --> 00:54.258
Take the stream. Now kindly go aw—

00:54.058 --> 00:55.258
[snores]

00:55.417 --> 00:57.657
Got a name, Old Shell?

00:58.307 --> 00:59.467
Yes.

01:00.733 --> 01:02.213
Easy! Big step!

01:02.433 --> 01:03.463
Bigger step.

01:03.783 --> 01:05.483
Much bigger step.

01:12.467 --> 01:13.667
[croak]

01:13.167 --> 01:14.367
Don't ask.

01:15.100 --> 01:16.730
So who's at the stone?

01:17.220 --> 01:18.220
A girl.

01:18.620 --> 01:22.280
She showed me the last one.

01:22.833 --> 01:25.103
Seventy-six years?

01:25.503 --> 01:28.313
Old Shell, humans forget.

01:29.658 --> 01:33.348
Then I'll remember for both of us.

01:39.383 --> 01:41.533
How long you been walking?

01:41.783 --> 01:42.783
Since spring.

01:43.542 --> 01:44.812
Since SPRING?!

01:44.862 --> 01:47.262
Okay. Feet! All four of them! Go, go, go!

01:48.100 --> 01:49.300
[gate creaks]

01:49.833 --> 01:51.713
Is this her house?

01:53.642 --> 01:54.642
I'm sorry.

01:55.800 --> 01:57.390
I promised.

02:04.658 --> 02:06.348
Old Shell.

02:06.598 --> 02:07.608
Look.

02:15.025 --> 02:17.705
Don't stop. I'll tell her you're coming.

02:20.117 --> 02:21.317
[hums]

02:24.227 --> 02:28.047
He's coming! He's very
slow, but he's coming!

02:28.050 --> 02:29.250
[gasps]

02:45.067 --> 02:46.947
Hello, Pebble.

02:48.108 --> 02:49.108
I'm here.

02:55.887 --> 02:56.997
PEBBLE?!

02:57.647 --> 02:58.897
She was six.

02:59.642 --> 03:01.182
You're late.

03:01.792 --> 03:02.902
I'm a tortoise.

03:02.942 --> 03:05.010
[laughs]

03:05.050 --> 03:09.930
I've climbed up here every summer.
In case you got the year wrong.

03:10.533 --> 03:12.773
Tortoises don't get the year wrong.

03:13.217 --> 03:14.357
I know.

03:14.857 --> 03:19.737
I just couldn't let you walk
all this way to an empty hill.

03:21.527 --> 03:22.727
[sniffs]

03:25.767 --> 03:28.237
Same time next comet?

03:28.987 --> 03:30.807
I'll start walking tomorrow.

03:30.847 --> 03:32.017
[laughs]

03:32.417 --> 03:34.357
I'm not coming.

03:35.257 --> 03:36.277
…I'm coming.

03:36.758 --> 03:40.678
And this time, nobody
climbed the hill alone.

03:41.058 --> 03:46.258
SEVENTY-SIX SUMMERS
